// MIMXRT1189 — Zephyr platform: the M0 CM33 platform + the EXTERNAL memories
// Zephyr's default board target links against.
//
// ⚠ WHAT THIS ADDS AND WHY IT IS HONEST:
// Zephyr's stock `mimxrt1180_evk/mimxrt1189/cm33` target uses
//     zephyr,sram   = &hyperram0     -> external HyperRAM  @ 0x14000000 (8 MiB)
//     zephyr,flash  = &w25q128jw     -> external NOR, XIP  @ 0x38000000 (16 MiB)
// Neither device is modelled here. What IS modelled is the MEMORY behind them:
// the image is placed by `sysbus LoadELF`, exactly as the boot ROM would have
// left an XIP image in place, so no flash protocol is exercised. This models the
// storage, NOT the FlexSPI/HyperBus devices -- a real scope limit, stated.
// ⭐ PARENTED ON m1, NOT cm33. The Zephyr harness runs on THIS platform, and it
// inherited the bare cm33 base -- so it had no LPADC, LPSPI, FlexCAN, GPT, LPTMR,
// RGPIO, RTWDOG or eDMA, while the board's own devicetree enables lpadc1, lpspi3,
// flexcan3, gpt2, lptmr1 and edma3/4. Zephyr's driver tests therefore ran against
// holes: adc_api and can/api printed NOTHING on Renode while QEMU produced 10 and
// 363 lines.
//
// ⚠ THE BLOCK AUDIT MISSED THIS BECAUSE OF HOW IT ASKED THE QUESTION. It counted
// instances across the UNION of all platforms and reported 22/22 families
// complete -- true, and useless here, because no single platform had them and the
// one the tests use had almost none. A capability present *somewhere* is not a
// capability present *where the firmware looks*.
using "mimxrt1189_m1.repl"

// FlexSPI1 NOR XIP window. 0x28000000, 16 MiB, secure alias 0x38000000. [brief]
// Zephyr links to the SECURE alias (measured: ELF LOAD at 0x38000000,
// entry 0x3800CBA5).
// ⚠ ONLY the secure alias. 0x28000000 is the FlexSPI controller's
// command-translated XIP window (see mimxrt1189_cm33.repl) and must stay that
// way for the SDK examples; Zephyr's cm33 image ELF-LOADs at 0x38000000, which
// needs to be plain writable memory. Mapping both here shadowed the controller
// window; mapping the controller window over both broke Zephyr. They are split.
flexspi1_xip: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x38000000
    size: 0x1000000

// External HyperRAM. Zephyr's zephyr,sram. 8 MiB at the secure alias
// 0x14000000 (= 0x04000000 + 0x1000_0000, the TZ-M secure offset [brief]);
// measured from the ELF's RW LOAD segments at 0x14000000/0x1400_0038.
hyperram0: Memory.MappedMemory @ {
        sysbus 0x04000000;
        sysbus 0x14000000
    }
    size: 0x800000

// ---- Board-init blocks the SDK examples needed, which Zephyr's ztest suites
// ---- also reach (hello_world did not, which is why they were missing here).
// Same models/values as mimxrt1189_m1.repl and _m2.repl.







// GPC_CPU_CTRL @ 0x44470000 (General Power Controller, per-CPU control) --
// reached by Zephyr's ztest init; observed read/write at 0x4447080C.
// Name checked against MIMXRT1189_cm33_COMMON.h (GPC_CPU_CTRL_BASE), NOT
// guessed -- my first comment here said BLK_CTRL_NS_AONMIX and was wrong.
// Register-backed window, no modelled behaviour.
gpc_cpu_ctrl: Miscellaneous.IMXRT1180_PeriphRdy @ sysbus 0x44470000

// NOTE: trdc1-3, dcdc, blkctrl_wakeupmix, src and blkctrl_s_aonmix are NOT
// declared here any more -- m1 already declares all seven at byte-identical
// type+base, and Renode rejects a redeclaration outright (Error E02: "Variable
// 'trdc1' was already declared"). Verified identical before deleting, so this
// removes duplication and changes no behaviour.
